Recently I read a small story about a mistress over-pampering her dog. That got a conversation started on our dinner table, "Should parents pamper their children?" Are you serious?!? Is that even a question?!?  It is awesome to be pampered! Of course, it has some bad things to it, but we'll get to that stuff later..... oh, maybe not. When people are pampering you, You basically get whatever you want! If you wanted to watch TV, you could watch TV. If you wanted to play video games, you could play video games. Isn't that the life that anyone would like?

Well, there is one bad thing about it. When you do not get what you want, you would most probably cry. This is from the lack of handling losses well. That is what is called being spoilt.

&nbsp;

This is a short story my friend Advaith and I made together.

Doughnut Boy had recently saved the universe and he was hoping for more excitement to happen around the world. “I’m bored. I wanna fight more crime.” Doughnut boy said sternly. He just wanted to get some fun around there. The next day while he was watching his daily news on his TV the news said, “Evil Mr. Nacho has invaded our city again! Doughnut Boy, please save us!”. That made Doughnut Boy bolt into his closet, put on his brand-new shoes, and run as fast as he could to the local news headquarters. When he reached there he said he would do the job of killing Mr. Nacho. When he reached to Mr. Nacho who was spreading his cheesy evilness all over the world! Then Mr. Nacho saw Doughnut Boy and he tried to spray his evilness on Doughnut Boy! Of course, he missed. Then on the next try Doughnut Boy took out his shaving mirror and it rebounded off of it! That killed Mr. Nacho and then Doughnut Boy celebrated with his friends as he had taken care of Mr. Nacho… at least for now!

<img class="alignnone" src="https://mastermuscle.files.wordpress.com/2012/08/doughnut.gif?w=490" alt="" width="292" height="282" /><strong>WAAAAAAAAAAAHHHHHHHHHHOOOOOOO!!!!!!!!!!</strong>

